The plan is not ready to establish production quality. Two concrete examples show why: the proposed link-narrowing code cannot fix a passage filed **only** under the wrong question, and rendering a numeric boundary cannot correct a boundary calculated from the wrong figure.

This was a read-only review. I checked the cited decisions, standard, response, plan, representative traces and code. I did **not** independently re-adjudicate all 126 census entries, and I did not run the pipeline or make paid calls. The severities below describe the production risk of the finding, not proof of its frequency.

## C1

**Coarse and fine answers — serious.** Claude is right that one result can settle both questions. D248’s general rule says “two questions are one when the same outcome settles both”; item 1 specifically combines wordings “whose final check is the same number.” A full interest-rate range can tell us whether the rate rose. Merely showing that “no increase” includes both a cut and no change does **not**, by itself, establish that the two questions must stay separate.

But the reverse shortcut is also unsupported: “same event on the same date” does not establish that the existing question retains the useful answer. A merged candidate inherits the existing question’s results and date. If the existing question records only “raise: yes/no,” it cannot express the size or direction of all the finer outcomes. D248 also requires separation when answers can move apart **and** an analyst would bet on each separately; the second condition has not been established for this pair. The probe pre-labelled the pair “same,” and its v4 responses split 2–1; that is not an independent answer to the disputed case.

**Cheapest check:** On the stored Fed pair and other stored coarse/fine pairs, independently identify the actual existing question’s possible results, whether they preserve the finer decision, and whether both warrant separate tracking. Replay the stored matching decisions through the real writer and inspect the surviving question, results and evidence. Include true alternate wordings as controls. **Verdict: partly.** Evidence: [D248](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2954), [standard §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:343), [probe’s pre-labelled pair](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/probe_collision_v4.py:25), [recorded results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/collision-v4-probe-2026-11-05-r2/results.json).

## C2

**Shared spending questions — serious.** The round-1 objection went too far if it treated four versus five companies alone as proof of a wrong merge. The standard explicitly says “同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据”; D190’s A17 specifically accepts the four-company figure as evidence for the five-company aggregate. D197 then assigns automatic identity to an admitted shared quantity by theme, measure and period.

Claude goes too far in the other direction. At seq 1250, the proposed question asks for **five companies’ total capital expenditure**, while v5 asks for **four companies’ data-center capital expenditure**. The difference is not only population: the spending measured also differs. The same trace’s `what_separates_it` identifies the population difference, and the recorded v4 reviewer identifies the spending-scope difference in all three draws. Those model responses are leads, not a final ruling that two questions must be kept. The standard’s condition is *the same aggregate*; it does not say every expenditure under the same theme is that aggregate.

The implementation has a concrete gap: preparation assigns broad `spend_total`, and [shared_key](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py:247) sets empty scope and makes the key without independently establishing that the candidates measure the same aggregate. This is the pair Claude asked for. It shows an **unproven automatic merge**, not yet a proven instruction to keep these two questions apart.

**Cheapest check:** Independently read the complete stored source and both questions’ actual result definitions, then replay seq 1250 through matching and the writer. In the same stored-data review, include D190 A17 as the required population-variant merge control and independently meaningful same-theme spending measures as counterexamples. Count false merges and missed merges. **Verdict: partly.** Evidence: [seq 1250](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1250.json), [standard §3 D](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:279), [D190](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2493), [D197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2551), [probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/collision-v4-probe-2026-11-05-r2/results.json).

## C3

**One passage linked to a new and an older-period question — serious.** Neither proposed blanket option is established. The existing filing rule says an estimate for another period goes to the old question **when no open question covers that period**, and also allows links to supported candidates. At seq 1207, B could not see A’s candidate because both read the same earlier snapshot. If A’s candidate survives as the appropriate home, retaining the older-period link solely as fallback can violate that rule. But a candidate may be dropped, merged or found not to cover the same quantity. Typing only its period cannot decide all of those questions, and deleting the old link before matching could leave useful evidence without a home.

**Cheapest check:** Replay the saved 1207 handover through matching and the real writer with the candidate surviving, merging and being rejected; inspect the final question identities, evidence links and drops. Also check a passage genuinely relevant to both questions. **Verdict: partly.** Evidence: [seq 1207](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-final-first100-2026-11-05/1207.json), [filing rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/placement.py:47), [D375](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4031).

## C4

**Research groups — blocker for the stated production contract.** The design already chooses the stage: extraction determines associations and returns structured declarations; matching and writing resolve and preserve them. The prototype supplies `group_refs: []` for every candidate and no new groups. Existing-group suggestions from Jev do not prove that a new continuing process can be declared.

The source does not require a group for every financial question. A should declare and associate groups **where the existing grouping contract calls for them**; moving group creation wholesale to a later matching step would depart from that contract.

**Cheapest check:** Replay stored candidates for an ongoing deal or product rollout and a plain company financial line through the real writer. Check that the former can create or join the appropriate group and the latter is not forced into one. **Verdict: disagree with treating the stage as undecided.** Evidence: [prototype](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py:297), [extraction grouping contract](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction.md:229), [standard’s group definition](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:263).

## C5

**Can the question eventually be checked? — serious.** A reason plus the name of a document is useful information, but it is not proof that the document will disclose the requested number. Seq 1251 asks for “the share of NVIDIA’s FY2028 revenue” from customers it financed and names the annual report. That does not establish that an annual report will identify all such customers and their revenue. Standard §4 asks whether a public item can put the answer into a result; it does not accept an arbitrary document name as proof.

The later November 5 decision changes admission: missing date, material, period or results must not automatically block a worthwhile sourced question. Therefore preparation may identify supported material and flag a known mismatch; it must not invent a source or turn a blank field into a rejection. Whether this particular share is demonstrably unavailable, as opposed to merely not established by the trace, requires inspecting the actual reporting basis.

**Cheapest check:** For seq 1251 and the other cited questions, have an independent reader inspect the source and relevant public reporting, and write what information would put each answer into a result. Distinguish “unknown,” “known not to be disclosed in that form,” and “supported”; replay how each is stored. **Verdict: partly.** Evidence: [seq 1251](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1251.json), [standard §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:313), [later decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4027).

## C6

**Deal sentence — serious.** Claude correctly restores the explicit exception: a not-yet-signed deal’s yes/no signing question can remain separate from an existing programme’s amount question. D210 distinguishes unsigned signing from an obligation already undertaken; D248 records that exception.

The proposed first sentence still says all agreement, approval and closing stages of a deal are one question. The cited exception alone does not prove that **every** such stage is interchangeable in every case, and collision-v4 also retains “a guarantee beside a financing” as a distinct-quantity example even though D248 item 1 expressly narrowed that earlier example. The two prompts and their examples need to be checked together against the actual D248 boundaries.

**Cheapest check:** Replay the stored signing-versus-programme-amount pair through A, matching and the writer; use a same-deal duplicate as a merge control. Inspect the existing and proposed results, not only the collision label. **Verdict: partly.** Evidence: [D210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2664), [D248 item 1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2954), [standard §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:343), [collision-v4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v4.txt:1).

## A-rows

These are assessments of the **proposed actions**, not claims that the fixes have been built or passed.

- **A1 — serious: partly.** Merging exact normalized quotes addresses that exact duplication mechanism and follows existing `sift`; it does not resolve different or contained quotations expressing the same research matter. Seq 1213 has two A passages and one combined B passage; a string-equality merge alone leaves overlap. A blind union of links also leaves C3 unresolved. No new rule is needed for exact duplicates, but the full “one matter” contract is not yet proved. Evidence: [seq 1213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1213.json), [sift](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/extraction.py:667), [standard §2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:263).

- **A2 — serious: partly.** Removing the part-year pace sentence addresses the demonstrated double-counting invitation. But “guidance, consensus or target, otherwise prior-year figure, otherwise no results” is a new closed list; the cited PRD requires a stated comparison and gives an example, not that exhaustive list. It could leave a useful question unjudged even where another supported comparison exists. Evidence: [Claude J1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r1/claude-findings.md:5), [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/06-views.md:78), [incomplete-details decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4027).

- **A3 — serious: partly.** Asking for the favourable end and ordering bounds addresses the inverted-label mechanism and is sourced to D186/D368. It does not prove that the model picked the correct favourable end, that the reference is right, or that existing readers preserve the new field. Those need a stored-data check across the affected readers. Evidence: [seq 1273](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1273.json), [D186](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2476).

- **A4 — serious: partly.** Rendering words from bounds removes a wording-versus-boundary disagreement, but it cannot fix bad arithmetic in the bounds. At seq 1280, the “within 5%” bounds are about $100 million wrong; rendering them faithfully would make the error consistent, not correct. Treating bounds as authoritative is an implementation choice, not proof that the model’s numeric values are right. Evidence: [seq 1280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1280.json), [census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r2/census-findings.json).

- **A5 — serious: partly.** Narrowing the em-dash normalization addresses the demonstrated risk of matching a changed number. The proposed “between two word characters” rule does not cover the cited `report—$96.2` example: `$` is not a word character. It is a new punctuation rule and needs positive and negative controls against stored quotes and summaries before it can be claimed to cover the class. Evidence: [comparison code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py:149), [round-1 attack](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r1/codex-attack.out).

- **A6 — serious: partly.** Refusing the run-on prevents the observed unsupported summary from being stored through that path, but also discards the supported sentence. D266 allowed retaining an exact copied sentence; a blanket refusal is a stricter new rule, not the same mechanism repaired. The three affected quotes need reading for lost useful information and all associated fields, not just quote validity. Evidence: [seq 1243](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1243.json), [response A6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r2/claude-responses.md:15).

- **A7 — serious: partly.** Matching the prepared year before applying the fiscal label fixes the demonstrated comparison-year case; it does not prove that the prepared year itself is the target period. The standard requires the correct period, not a first-year text heuristic. Check target and comparison years in both orders, including a wrong or absent prepared year. Evidence: [current `question_year`](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py:239), [standard §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:322).

- **A8 — serious: partly.** Applying a supported period limit independently of whether results exist addresses the bypass at [handover](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py:288). But the plan’s “obligations within 18 months” flattens D210: an **already undertaken** obligation is checked at the next annual filing; the 18-month signing rule concerns an unsigned obligation. Nor does the old `check_admission`, which refuses missing settling material, directly implement the later optional-details decision. Re-derive known, unknown, signed and unsigned cases; do not restore an old gate wholesale. Evidence: [D210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2664), [old check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/extraction.py:523), [later decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4027).

- **A9 — serious: partly.** Correct to seek Alex’s decision on a general analyst check-date policy: the standard explicitly permits a labelled fiscal-year-end check for an undated pending regulatory decision, but does not establish the proposed annual-report-month rule for every financial question. The later decision permits an estimate and says its arrival alone does **not** resolve a question. Setting dates without examining pull-mode closure would therefore introduce a new lifecycle rule. The 22 empty dates establish a gap, not that all 22 should be auto-filled. Evidence: [seq 1237](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1237.json), [standard §3 E](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:280), [later decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4027).

- **A10 — blocker: partly.** Claude correctly identifies the missing mechanism, but leaves its owner open despite the existing extraction-time contract. See C4. Evidence: [prototype](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py:297), [grouping contract](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction.md:229).

- **A11 — serious: partly.** Held-out inputs and the unchanged ruler are necessary, but the stated action does not itself measure missed questions, missed evidence, attribution, cost, latency or actual daily decisions. The frozen judgement scorer also requires the seed fixture; how that relates to the unseeded product-shaped run remains a decision. No new standard is justified by these limitations. Evidence: [blind-question packet](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/blind-questions-confirm-2026-11-05/prompt-1.txt), [plan v1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v1.md:61).

- **A12 — serious: partly.** An admission reason and a named document do not establish source support or that the document resolves the question. The later decision also forbids rejecting merely because the material is unknown. See C5. Evidence: [seq 1251](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1251.json), [standard §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:313).

- **A13 — serious: partly.** A prompt audit is the required next investigation, not a demonstrated fix or proof of the mechanism. The errors span preparation **and B**: seq 1277 attributes a reported claim to SK hynix, while the passage attributes it to a Korean outlet. The response mentions preparation alone; plan v1 later names both. Audit both whole requests against the source and inspect all affected written fields. Evidence: [seq 1277](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1277.json), [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408).

- **A14 — serious: disagree that the named code fixes the class.** `narrowest_links` only removes an ancestor when **both** the narrower question and its parent are already linked. It cannot discover a narrower home when B linked only the broad question, nor establish semantic relevance where no dependency exists. Seq 1211’s hyperscaler revenue linked to total revenue is therefore not shown to be fixed by calling it. The fallback is an existing decision; changing it requires the proposed decision, but blaming it alone does not explain all wrong links. Evidence: [seq 1211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1211.json), [`narrowest_links`](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/extraction.py:55), [filing rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/placement.py:47).

## Missed

- **Whole filing cut off — blocker for claiming the full-item contract.** At seq 1280, the later purchase-commitments note says agreements cover inventory and non-inventory items “primarily through the next 12 months” and remaining commitments were “$34.2 billion.” The prototype cuts A, B and preparation at 400,000 characters, so that later detail is not sent. An earlier passage does contain the $34.2 billion figure, so the trace does **not** prove truncation caused the missed question. It does prove the full-item requirement was not met. Count all stored items crossing the limit and what is lost before proposing a remedy. **Verdict: disagree with the response’s omission.** Evidence: [seq 1280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1280.json), [request construction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py:31), [full-item requirement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction.md:154).

- **A lower bound becomes a bounded prediction — serious.** At seq 1249 the source says “more than $200 billion”; the judgement selects the $200–250 billion result. Seq 1253 similarly selects $40–45 billion from guidance “above $40 billion.” Removing pace references, ordering labels and rendering bounds do not establish why the judge may infer those upper bounds. Plan v1 mentions a floor-as-point test, but its proposed preparation fixes do not show that the frozen judge will stop making the inference. Inspect the cited judgement requests and reasons, including what other evidence supports each selection. **Verdict: partly; named in the plan, not resolved by its mechanism.** Evidence: [seq 1249](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1249.json), [seq 1253](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1253.json), [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408).

- **Meaning errors beyond attribution — serious.** At seq 1280, the passage describes an **increase** in billing of $15,261.5 million; B’s summary can read as $15.3 billion of total billing. At seq 1223, a conditional FY2028 forecast is recorded as a period “not specified,” despite the period in the sentence. These are separate from choosing the wrong speaker and are not covered by A13 as written. **Verdict: disagree with the response’s omission.** Evidence: [seq 1280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1280.json), [seq 1223](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1223.json), [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408).

- **A broad figure filed as a narrow obligation — serious.** At seq 1210, $279 billion is described as supply commitments “primarily” about memory; it is filed under the memory-and-advanced-packaging amount. “Primarily” does not make the whole total that narrower amount. A14’s broad-revenue examples do not address this different scope error. The passage may be relevant evidence if the distinction is preserved; the trace does not justify treating the whole number as the answer. **Verdict: disagree with the response’s omission.** Evidence: [seq 1210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1210.json), [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408).

- **The plan’s counts are not reconciled — serious.** The response says **9 exact duplicate groups** in confirmation; plan v1 says **10 statements** plus contained quotes. The census contains differently named and overlapping duplicate findings, so those numbers may count different units. Likewise the census has eight entries labelled invented-statement-date while the plan reports seven. Neither discrepancy proves which count is correct. Name the unit, deduplicate by trace and passage, and show the list before presenting a class size or the share a fix removes. **Verdict: partly; the issue is noticed, but the counts are not auditable as presented.** Evidence: [response A1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r2/claude-responses.md:10), [plan table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v1.md:8), [census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r2/census-findings.json).

- **Written questions are not the same as judged questions — serious.** The round-1 review reports 22 written questions, six without results, and 14 with a recorded judgement during the observed window. Seq 1213’s FY2028 revenue question has no results or judgement. This is permitted by the later decision, but a count of accepted questions or structurally valid results is not evidence that daily judging worked or was correct. The response’s measurement row does not explicitly carry this distinction into its acceptance test. **Verdict: partly.** Evidence: [seq 1213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1213.json), [judging eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:284), [round-1 attack](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r1/codex-attack.out).

The next reviewable step is to reconcile the stored findings by actual passage and mechanism, then prove the handover on the real writer—including overlapping passages, candidate survival and the correct final links. The present plan should not claim that its proposed checks already settle those outcomes.